      (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) hide)
    )
    (property "Note" "IO3/IO45/IO46 are strapping pins, each with a 10k pull-down -- anything attached must not fight them at boot. Pins 4 and 5 are no longer spare: IO15 is the power-fail interrupt and IO16 is the sensor-rail enable. They stay on the header as probe points, so the ride-through can be watched on a scope without unsoldering anything, but nothing else may drive them. The ground pin is here so a probe or a ribbon has a return" (at 271.78 240.76 0)
      (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) hide)
    )
